      "body": "## Motivation\n\nQwen3 with TP2/DCP2 can fail during KV-cache writes because its projections produce four K/V heads while the cache expects eight.\nFA3 also lacks the non-MLA DCP cache and attention handling.\nThese unsupported combinations currently reach execution instead of reporting a configuration error.\n\n## Modifications\n\nReject `--dcp-size > 1` for `Qwen3ForCausalLM` and for non-MLA models that resolve either attention phase to FA3.\nRaise a startup `ValueError` with `--dcp-size 1` as the workaround.\nUse resolved backends so defaults and separate prefill/decode selections receive the same validation.\n\nAdd one regression test for Qwen3 with TP2/DCP2 and FA3.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo model or kernel changes.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThe change only affects startup validation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #34874793157](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34874793157)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #34874792824](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34874792824)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:start -->:x: [Run #34874792973](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/34874792973)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd-rocm720:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
